# {{project_name}}

A MuduDB application written in C, compiled to a WebAssembly component with
a freestanding clang build and `wasm-tools`, packaged as
`{{module_name}}.mpk`. Scaffolded with `mpm-crate` — edit this project
freely; it is a starting point, not a generated artifact.

It defines three tables (`items`, `item_info`, `item_info_labels`, see
`sql/ddl.sql`) and two Mudu Procedures (see `src/procedures.c`):
`create_item` (scalar arguments) and `update_item_info`, which demonstrates
a **user-defined record type** — the `item-info` record declared in
`wit/types.wit` — as a procedure parameter and return type.

## Prerequisites

- A clang able to target **wasm32 freestanding**: the
  [wasi-sdk](https://github.com/WebAssembly/wasi-sdk) clang is used by
  default (`~/.wasi-sdk/wasi-sdk-29.0`; override with
  `WASI_SDK=/path/to/wasi-sdk cargo make`, or `CLANG=/path/to/clang`).
  Only the compiler and the sysroot *headers* are used — the build is
  `-nostdlib`, so no libc is linked.
- `cargo-make` (`cargo install cargo-make`) and `wasm-tools` (`cargo install
  wasm-tools`).
- `mgen`, `mtp`, `mpm-build` — the MuduDB toolchain; `mpm-install`,
  `mudud`, `mcli` to install and invoke the package.

## Layout

- `sql/ddl.sql` — database schema; `sql/init.sql` — seed data.
- `src/procedures.c` — hand-written procedures; SQL runs through
  `src/mudu_sys.h` / `src/mudu_sys.c` (MSSP framing) over the
  `mududb:api/system` byte pipe. Each procedure is a non-`static`
  `mudu_proc_fn`-shaped function (`int fn(const mudu_proc_param *,
  mudu_datum *, mudu_error *)`) with a `// mudu-proc (name: type, ...) ->
  type` comment immediately above it. The annotation carries the wire
  signature (the C declaration has no usable type information); annotation
  types are `i64`, `f64`, `string`, `option<T>` for nullable parameters,
  and the user-defined record/enum type names registered via
  `mtp --type-wit wit/types.wit` (`MUDU_DATUM_RECORD` for records,
  `MUDU_DATUM_I64` ordinals for enums). The session OID is implicit in
  `mudu_proc_param.session` and never appears in the annotation.
- `wit/types.wit` — the project's message types (the `item-info` record),
  consumed two ways: `mgen message` turns it into the `gentypes/Types.h`
  header, and `mtp --type-wit` registers the names so procedure annotations
  may use them. The `package` clause is required: one WIT directory is one
  package, and the `wasm-tools component embed` world build rejects
  headerless files sitting next to a packaged world.
- `gentypes/Types.h` — **generated by mgen** (`cargo make gentypes`): the
  `item_info` struct plus its `item_info_encode`/`item_info_decode` codecs
  as one self-contained header (the same shape the binding's
  `mududb/types/Uni*.h` carry). Never edit by hand.
- `generated/entity/<table>.h` — **generated by mgen** (`cargo make
  generate`, from `sql/ddl.sql`): one self-contained header per table —
  the `<table>_row` struct, the row/`mudu_datum` codecs and the typed
  `<table>_insert` / `<table>_get_by_pk` / `<table>_delete_by_pk` helpers
  the procedures build on. Nullable columns carry a `<name>_is_null`
  flag; strings are `mudu_string` byte slices. Never edit by hand.
- `generated/procedures_gen.c` — **generated by mtp** (`cargo make
  transpile`): per procedure an `extern` declaration, a static arity/kind
  check preamble, and the `mp2-<kebab-proc>` export wrapper driving
  `mudu_run_proc`. Never edit by hand.
- `src/mudu_sys.c` — the syscall layer: SyscallPayload v1 (MSSP) frames
  encoded/decoded with the binding's `uni_syscall_*` codecs, the procedure
  byte-pipe shapes (including the `MUDU_DATUM_RECORD` passthrough for
  user-defined record parameters/returns), and the minimal freestanding
  runtime (bump allocator, `cabi_realloc`, the `realloc`/`free` shims
  behind the binding's `mp_realloc`, `memcpy` & friends — there is no
  libc).
- `src/mududb/` — the vendored MuduDB C binding (a byte-copy snapshot):
  `codec/mpack.{h,c}` (the MessagePack runtime + decode arena),
  `codec/mpack_alloc.c` (the default `mp_realloc`),
  `codec/record_bridge.{h,c}` (the bridge between the record-case envelope
  and the generated record codecs) and `types/Uni*.h` (the generated Uni*
  types/codecs).
- `wit/world.wit` — **generated by mtp**: the component world, `import
  mududb:api/system` plus one `mp2-<kebab-proc>` export per procedure.
  `wit/deps/mududb-api/api.wit` is a copy of the host syscall interface.
- `package/package.cfg.json` — package metadata.
- `package/package.desc.json` — **generated by mtp**: the procedure
  signatures (procedure and parameter names are the snake_case wire names
  from the annotation); a record parameter is described with the host's
  `Record` type family, the WIT field names verbatim as the JSON keys.

Adding a procedure means writing the function plus its `// mudu-proc`
annotation and rebuilding — the export wrappers, the world WIT and the
descriptor stay in sync because all three come from the same source.

## Records on the wire

A record argument travels as the positional `uni-data-value` record case
(field order = WIT declaration order, names dropped by the host). The
procedure decodes it with `mp_record_bridge_write` (serializes the
envelope as the integer-keyed MessagePack map the generated codecs read)
composed with `item_info_decode`, and encodes a record result
symmetrically with `item_info_encode` + `mp_record_bridge_read`. Rules of
the JSON/desc surface:

- **JSON keys = WIT field names, verbatim** (`in-stock`, not `in_stock`).
- **Booleans cross as 0/1** — the host has no boolean data-type family, so
  a WIT `bool` field is described as `I32` and takes JSON `0`/`1`.
- **u32/u16/u8 fields cross as i32**; missing JSON fields are an error,
  unknown keys are tolerated. u128/i128 record fields are rejected by the
  C bridge (no 128-bit record codec in the C backend).

`update_item_info` stores the record flattened into the `item_info` table
(the label list as `item_info_labels` side rows keyed by `(item_id,
idx)`), updating the row by key and inserting it on first write.

## Build

```bash
cargo make package
```

This runs `mgen entity` (generate) → `mgen check-sql` → `mgen message`
(gentypes) → `mtp c` (transpile) → `clang --target=wasm32 -nostdlib
-mexec-model=reactor` →
`wasm-tools component embed` / `component new` (generates the canonical-ABI
glue; no `--adapt` needed since the module imports nothing outside the
world) → `wasm-tools validate` → `mpm-build create`, producing
`target/wasm32-wasip2/release/{{module_name}}.mpk`. The component file is
named `{{module_name}}.wasm` so its stem matches the `{{module_name}}`
module in `package/package.desc.json` (an `mpm-build` requirement).

## Install and invoke

Start `mudud`, then:

```bash
mpm-install target/wasm32-wasip2/release/{{module_name}}.mpk

mcli --addr 127.0.0.1:9527 --http-addr 127.0.0.1:8300 app-invoke \
  --app {{module_name}} --module {{module_name}} --proc create_item \
  --json '{"item_id": 2, "name": "pear"}'

# the record procedure: nested JSON, WIT field names verbatim, bool as 0/1
mcli --addr 127.0.0.1:9527 --http-addr 127.0.0.1:8300 app-invoke \
  --app {{module_name}} --module {{module_name}} --proc update_item_info \
  --json '{"item_id": 2, "info": {"name": "pear", "price": 199, "in-stock": 1, "labels": ["fresh", "green"]}}'
```

## Extending

- Add a procedure: write a non-`static` `mudu_proc_fn` in `src/procedures.c`
  with a `// mudu-proc (name: type, ...) -> type` annotation comment
  immediately above it, and rebuild. mtp regenerates the export wrappers,
  `wit/world.wit` and `package/package.desc.json` from the annotations.
- Add a table: extend `sql/ddl.sql` (and optionally `sql/init.sql`) and
  rebuild — `mgen entity` regenerates the typed headers and `mgen
  check-sql` validates the SQL string literals in `src/procedures.c`
  against the DDL.
- Add a record type: declare it in `wit/types.wit` and rebuild — `mgen
  message` regenerates `gentypes/Types.h` and mtp resolves the name in
  procedure annotations.

## Compiling as C++

The same sources also compile as C++ — the headers have `extern "C"`
guards and the code avoids C99-only constructs. To build with clang++
instead (adding `-fno-exceptions -fno-rtti` keeps the module free of
unwinding support imports), first `cargo make transpile`, then:

```bash
"${WASI_SDK:-$HOME/.wasi-sdk/wasi-sdk-29.0}/bin/clang++" \
  --target=wasm32 -x c++ -nostdlib -mexec-model=reactor -O2 \
  -fno-exceptions -fno-rtti \
  -isystem "${WASI_SDK:-$HOME/.wasi-sdk/wasi-sdk-29.0}/share/wasi-sysroot/include/wasm32-wasip1" \
  -I. -Isrc -Igenerated/entity -Wl,--no-entry -Wl,--export-memory \
  src/mududb/codec/mpack.c src/mududb/codec/mpack_alloc.c \
  src/mududb/codec/record_bridge.c \
  src/mudu_sys.c src/procedures.c generated/procedures_gen.c \
  -o build/c/procedures.core.wasm
```

then re-run `cargo make c-embed c-component validate-component package`.
